# Arguments for the limut HUB75 display. Installed to /etc/default/limut-hub75.
#
# install.sh will NOT overwrite this file once it exists: the wall is a property of the room,
# not of the checkout. Copy it by hand after changing it here.
#
# The wall as built and verified 2026-09-04: six P5 64x32 modules, each mounted rotated 90
# degrees, in two side-by-side full-height columns of three -- a 64 x 192 portrait wall.
# See draw/hub75/CLAUDE.md for where every number below comes from.
#
#   --size 64x192      what limut renders: the wall in portrait, the right way up
#   --canvas 1280x512  the card's SCREEN, which LEDVISION did not change. The receiving card
#                      window is a 192x64 cabinet at the origin, but the card will not latch a
#                      frame until a whole screen has gone out, so the full height is still sent
#   --trim-canvas      ...but only the 192 columns the wall occupies. Every row still goes, in
#                      order, which is the rule the card actually enforces. 514 packets/frame
#                      instead of 1538: 18 MB/s and a solid 60 fps, against 120 MB/s and 46 fps
#   --row-map 1        the card scans 1/16, matching the panels. It did NOT before the card was
#                      reconfigured, when this had to be 2
#   --panel            each module: its region in the RENDER, its cell in the CANVAS, and rot 90
#                      to undo the mounting. Derived from the `cellid` pattern, 2026-09-04
#   --brightness 100   six modules at full white is ~120 W, i.e. 24 A at 5 V. Raise this only
#                      after checking the supply and the wiring can survive a white frame
#   --gamma 2.2        the running value; draw/hub75/pi/pixel-check.js needs --gamma 1 instead
#
# Deliberately absent, because each silently swallows a visual bound from limut: --output raw,
# --no-gpu, and --test-pattern (a pattern replaces the layer entirely).

HUB75_ARGS=--name hub75-01 --output colorlight --iface eth0 --size 64x192 --canvas 1280x512 --trim-canvas --row-map 1 --color-order bgr --brightness 100 --gamma 2.2 --panel 0,128:0,0:64x32:90 --panel 0,64:64,0:64x32:90 --panel 0,0:128,0:64x32:90 --panel 32,128:0,32:64x32:90 --panel 32,64:64,32:64x32:90 --panel 32,0:128,32:64x32:90
